{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02268",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.75,
      "end_seconds": 6.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.26,
      "end_seconds": 12.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 13.02,
      "end_seconds": 18.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.07,
      "end_seconds": 28.88,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "Yeah, um, it's an ulcer under the big toe. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.8,
      "end_seconds": 31.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.87,
      "end_seconds": 35.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Probably about four days. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.77,
      "end_seconds": 41.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.37,
      "end_seconds": 45.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "I, I'd say mild"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.04,
      "end_seconds": 50.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "okay, does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.8,
      "end_seconds": 61.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.59,
      "text": "yeah, it usually comes with a red swollen foot i've also been feeling shivery, for about four days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.4,
      "end_seconds": 67.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.71,
      "end_seconds": 81.91,
      "duration_seconds": 13.2,
      "text": "Let me think, I'd say all the time. I'd give it a six, out of ten. The red swollen foot? That's been since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.58,
      "end_seconds": 87.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "and what about black skin, tracking redness or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.84,
      "end_seconds": 93.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "hmm, no, I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.88,
      "end_seconds": 97.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "How about pain in the foot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.85,
      "end_seconds": 109.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "okay, you know, so I haven't noticed any pain in the foot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.65,
      "end_seconds": 113.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.44,
      "end_seconds": 118.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Actually, you know, no, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.73,
      "end_seconds": 137.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.6,
      "end_seconds": 145.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Cat fur. I come out in... well, sneezing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.48,
      "end_seconds": 152.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.4,
      "end_seconds": 156.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Diabetes, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.88,
      "end_seconds": 164.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Alright, diabetes, that matches what I have here. Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.52,
      "end_seconds": 168.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.77,
      "end_seconds": 170.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.6,
      "end_seconds": 177.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.46,
      "end_seconds": 181.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.55,
      "end_seconds": 187.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.7,
      "end_seconds": 205.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "So, what do you take on a a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.94,
      "end_seconds": 213.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "I mean, uh, I'm on metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.28,
      "end_seconds": 219.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "can I check a a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.92,
      "end_seconds": 232.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.99,
      "end_seconds": 254.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 119 over 66, pulse is 105 beats a a minute, temperature 38.4."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.7,
      "end_seconds": 261.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Mm, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.17,
      "end_seconds": 264.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.29,
      "end_seconds": 272.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Right, I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.64,
      "end_seconds": 276.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "fine by me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.89,
      "end_seconds": 280.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "take a a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.5,
      "end_seconds": 300.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "The ulcer is deep to the fat with surrounding redness and the foot pulses are present."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.77,
      "end_seconds": 304.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.87,
      "end_seconds": 310.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "That's all I needed to to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.35,
      "end_seconds": 349.8,
      "duration_seconds": 32.45,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be an infected diabetic foot ulcer, or it might be osteomyelitis. Let's book an X-ray of the foot to look into possible osteomyelitis. What I'm giving you is co-amoxiclav, 625 milligrams, three times a day, seven days. That should help with infected ulcer. Keep the weight off the foot and keep the dressing dry. I think the diabetic foot clinic should see you too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.66,
      "end_seconds": 354.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I mean, sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.6,
      "end_seconds": 361.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "We'll catch up in two days. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.54,
      "end_seconds": 367.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "So, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}